  "answer": "The higher-authority business evidence is the segment analysis in [NL-016-S03], which supersedes the sales-playbook emphasis on education startups. It supports prioritizing regulated mid-market and enterprise customers, not SMB/education startups: mid-market (28 accounts) and enterprise (9 accounts) together generate 83.8% of recurring revenue, with lower monthly churn (2.1% mid-market, 1.3% enterprise vs 4.8% SMB), higher NPS (47 and 52 vs 31), and stronger LTV:CAC ratios (enterprise 16.0x vs SMB 8.3x) [NL-016-S03]. That same evidence explicitly states that the previous sales playbook highlighting education startups is contradicted by metrics showing weaker long-term retention for smaller startups like EduVantage Labs [NL-016-S03], [NL-015-S03].\n\nThe trade-off is longer, more complex onboarding: mid-market takes a median of 5.2 weeks and enterprise 8.7 weeks due to permission and security complexities, and enterprise average CAC is $22,000 [NL-016-S03]. This slower, costlier sales cycle is the cost of pursuing the higher-value regulated segment.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
